    "Trade Marks Act 1995",
    "Part 21—Miscellaneous",
    "Division 1—Applications and other documents",
    "213B  Directions by Registrar for filing of documents"
  ],
  "instrument": "TMA1995",
  "kind": "section",
  "number": "213B",
  "ref": "TMA1995/s213B",
  "text": "(1) The Registrar may, by writing, give a direction specifying the form in which a document is to be filed under this Act. Note 1: A reference to this Act includes the regulations (see section 6). Note 2: See also paragraph 231(2)(ba) (about regulations). (2) Subsection (1) does not apply in relation to a document that is required to be in an approved form. (3) The Registrar must publish the direction in accordance with the regulations. (4) A direction under subsection (1) is not a legislative instrument.",
